{"schema":"forgedock.review-event/v1","eventId":"3466851c-ee12-40b8-838b-b998586c5bd7","reviewId":"review-ae1b8c6f-d865-44db-8e6e-a5c23391a6b5","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":5,"previousEventHash":"sha256:7e059e844059c89e8497f3d6fed54e5d1803ea844b2af938e676f35913bc7ab4","type":"review.findings-recorded","occurredAt":"2026-08-27T05:26:43.046Z","idempotencyKey":"panel:1:findings","payload":{"round":1,"findings":[{"id":"correctness-1","reviewer":"forge-review-correctness","runId":"review-ae1b8c6f-d865-44db-8e6e-a5c23391a6b5","headSha":"a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"medium","category":"correctness","file":"src/adapters/verification-preflight.ts","line":199,"summary":"Malformed npm run commands can bypass package-script validation","evidence":["packageScriptName now returns script || undefined for npm run instead of rejecting when no script is named.","preflightRequiredVerificationCommands only calls assertPackageScript when a script name is returned, so a required command such as npm run --silent is accepted and executes npm script-listing behavior rather than the configured verification script.","The removed tests previously covered npm run with no script and asserted rejection; replacement tests do not cover this path."]},{"id":"correctness-2","reviewer":"forge-review-correctness","runId":"review-ae1b8c6f-d865-44db-8e6e-a5c23391a6b5","headSha":"a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3","confidence":"likely","severity":"medium","category":"correctness","file":"src/agents/child-runtime.ts","line":1941,"summary":"Investigation label projection no longer recognizes valid non-uppercase verdict formatting","evidence":["The previous implementation used a case-insensitive regex allowing whitespace and both decompose/decomposed, then passed the parsed outcome to canonical mapping.","The replacement checks only exact **Verdict**: INVALID; lowercase or whitespace-variant INVALID and every DECOMPOSED verdict fall through to workflow:ready-to-build.","An investigation report with **Verdict**: DECOMPOSED or normal lowercase formatting can therefore project a build-ready label instead of invalid/decomposed, changing workflow routing."]},{"id":"security-001","reviewer":"forge-review-security","runId":"review-ae1b8c6f-d865-44db-8e6e-a5c23391a6b5","headSha":"a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3","confidence":"likely","severity":"medium","category":"security","file":"src/adapters/github-projection.ts","line":192,"summary":"setWorkflowLabel no longer validates issueNumber before interpolating it into the GitHub API path","evidence":["The previous positive safe-integer check was removed from setWorkflowLabel.","The changed code directly constructs `${this.#apiRoot}/issues/${issueNumber}` and `${this.#apiRoot}/issues/${issueNumber}/labels`; JavaScript callers or deserialized state can supply non-number values despite the TypeScript annotation, allowing path/query characters or malformed values to reach the transport.","projectEvent and #addMissingLabels retain the same validation/normalization pattern, demonstrating that this method's removed guard is a regression rather than an intentional API contract change."]}]}}
